}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"52eef4c1-167f-4acf-8b57-78b280bcd971"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Surface-like graphs", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"02f250af-893d-487c-bdc2-e9a4992129f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TessellationCurvature",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the combinatorial Gaussian curvature at a vertex of a regular \
or uniform map; its sign says spherical, flat or hyperbolic"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"6ea781a0-cf8d-4b37-ad86-cb28e77b87b8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TessellationEulerCharacteristic",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the Euler characteristic V - E + F of a tessellation graph"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"701b2e9b-54d2-4c68-8275-a1627fb2a9ca"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["TessellationGenus",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the orientable genus of a tessellation graph, from its Euler \
characteristic"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"d73357a7-a7b8-45a8-921d-3030208c141b"],

Cell["\<\
waits: a test whether a graph is surface-like at a scale, its metric balls \
discs and its metric shells cycles\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"36fbc551-1be4-4773-8a08-e8e88a19702e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Preparing a substrate", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"e0516ffe-ca6c-4645-ad68-e9a531b689f9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["CenterGraph",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] the substrate cut to a fraction q of the way out from its \
centre"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"d3e6f48f-ac1a-43b2-8c25-9cc43aa642d5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["BoundarylessGraph",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " \[LongDash] deletes every edge joining two rim vertices and then the \
vertices this isolates, an open window onto the geometry"
}], "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"eb9621f7-d4a0-4b27-b75e-b7b1c3ef6d68"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["GraphExteriorBoundary",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
